{"page":"ADGRL3","gene":"ADGRL3","accession":"Q9HAR2","protein":"Adhesion G protein-coupled receptor L3","length":1447,"events":["Alternative splicing"],"canonical":{"accession":"Q9HAR2-1","name":"1","synonyms":[],"notes":[{"topic":"Function","text":"Orphan adhesion G protein-coupled receptor (aGPCR), which mediates synapse specificity. Ligand binding causes a conformation change that triggers signaling via guanine nucleotide-binding proteins (G proteins) and modulates the activity of downstream effectors, such as adenylate cyclase. Isoform 1 is specifically coupled to G(s) G proteins and mediates activation of adenylate cyclase activity. Following G protein-coupled receptor activation, undergoes liquid-liquid phase transition, associates with (1) cell adhesion molecules that are expressed at the surface of adjacent cells, as well as (2) PDZ-containing proteins, such as SHANK3 and DLG4, in the cytoplasm to direct synapse formation"},{"topic":"Subunit","text":"Interacts (via PDZ-binding motif) with SHANK3. Interacts (via PDZ-binding motif) with DLG4"}],"transcripts":{"ensembl":[],"refseq":["NM_001387537.1","NM_001387538.1","NM_001387539.1"],"refseqProteins":["NP_001374466.1","NP_001374467.1","NP_001374468.1"],"maneSelect":false},"model":{"entry":"AF-Q9HAR2-F1","cif":"https://alphafold.ebi.ac.uk/files/AF-Q9HAR2-F1-model_v6.cif","meanPlddt":69.3,"plddt":[[0,2],[50,1],[0,1],[50,13],[0,10],[50,1],[70,2],[90,14],[70,6],[90,12],[70,1],[90,1],[70,1],[90,1],[70,9],[90,5],[70,1],[90,11],[70,3],[90,7],[70,2],[90,7],[70,1],[90,10],[70,3],[50,5],[70,4],[90,1],[70,2],[90,2],[70,1],[90,3],[70,2],[90,17],[70,5],[90,66],[70,2],[90,3],[70,1],[90,53],[70,1],[90,31],[70,5],[50,6],[70,2],[90,8],[70,2],[90,11],[70,4],[90,29],[70,2],[50,2],[0,99],[50,2],[70,3],[90,2],[70,5],[90,3],[70,7],[90,5],[70,3],[90,9],[70,3],[50,1],[70,9],[90,1],[70,1],[90,7],[70,1],[90,2],[70,1],[90,2],[70,9],[90,10],[70,2],[90,17],[70,19],[90,16],[70,6],[90,1],[70,6],[90,14],[70,1],[90,3],[70,1],[90,2],[70,8],[90